        "TXXX": [
          "lyrics-eng [Verse 1]\nI saw the pictures underneath the trees\nTwo little piles where they shouldn't be\nSomeone said the city had been told\nAnd suddenly the whole damn story broke\nThe angry faces started coming in\nCalling out the workers for their sins\nI watched the comments gather one by one\nAnd knew exactly what had to be done\n[Pre-Chorus]\nYou said somebody had to care\nI said somebody better prepare\n[Chorus]\nDamn, thank God the city was notified\nBefore another wheelbarrow arrived\nTwo were enough to bring this town to its knees\nConcrete underneath the evergreen trees\nAnd I don't know how we made it through\nThe things those two small wheelbarrows put us through\nBut I'll remember where I was somehow\nWhen we almost lost the whole damn town\n[Verse 2]\nOne said the workers must be lazy men\nAnother swore they'd do it all again\nThen someone asked if they were building a dam\nAnd that's when everything got out of hand\nI wore the angry face just like the rest\nDelivered every word with righteousness\nLike somewhere sirens echoed through the night\nFor two small loads that didn't look quite right\n[Pre-Chorus]\nYou called it rude, you called the city hall\nI wondered if we'd survive at all\n[Chorus]\nDamn, thank God the city was notified\nBefore another wheelbarrow arrived\nTwo were enough to bring this town to its knees\nConcrete underneath the evergreen trees\nAnd I don't know how we made it through\nThe things those two small wheelbarrows put us through\nBut I'll remember where I was somehow\nWhen we almost lost the whole damn town\n[Bridge]\nMaybe someday the grass will grow again\nMaybe time will heal Big Dipper Park, my friend\nMaybe children will return without fear\nAnd tell the story of what happened here\nBut there's one thought that keeps me up at night\nOne possibility I can't leave behind—\nWhat if nobody had made that call?\nWhat if there'd been...\na third one after all?\n[Final Chorus]\nDamn, thank God the city was notified\nWe were one wheelbarrow from the other side\nHold your loved ones close and don't forget\nThe greatest threat this little town has met\nYeah, somehow we all made it through\nThose horrifying wheelbarrows, number one and two\nAnd every August I'll remember how\nWe nearly lost the whole damn town\n[Outro]\nTwo small wheelbarrows beneath the trees\nThoughts and prayers for the community ",
          "sga 0.8 ",
